{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The governing measurement is the trace, and on it a deviation exists but is plainly non-material: gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 22.95 km against the stored optimal of 16.7 km gives an excess of 6.25 km, or 37.4%, so both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (6.25 km > 0.8 km; 37.4% > 20%), but both materiality limbs fail (6.25 km is short of the 8.0 km absolute bar; 37.4% is short of the 50% bar). The deviation is therefore NOT material, POL-RD-06's driver_profile check is not engaged, and neither the FULL_REFUND uplift in POL-RD-06(b) nor the driver-conduct referral in POL-RD-06(c) may issue against this driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02830", "EV-TRIP-02830"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if POL-RD-06's driver_profile check were run, the only two counters that clause names show no pattern: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1, below the 3-flag trigger, and 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 395 is a rate of 0.0025, an order of magnitude below the 0.05 trigger and with the 40-trip floor satisfied. No pattern is established, so no uplift and no conduct referral follows. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is a near-synonym and is not the trailing-90-day figure this clause asks for; substituting it is forbidden by POL-GEN-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02830"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On this METERED fare the remedy is arithmetic and cannot be inflated: charged_total is 30.18; recomputed_fare is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 16.7 + 0.28 x 22.5) x the surge_multiplier of 1.0 read from the fare_breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee = 23.425, with no ERP, no fixed surcharge, no waiting_time_fee and no promo discount; the refund before rounding is 30.18 - 23.425 = 6.755, rounded UP to a payable 6.80. That is 22.4% of charged_total, far below the 90% share that would convert the outcome to a FULL_REFUND, and it is 1.70 below the 8.50 the rider contests. The outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of 6.80, not the whole amount claimed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02830", "EV-TRIP-02830"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing may be added on top of that figure: fare_breakdown.erp_lines total 0.00 with no off-optimal-route gantry charged, and no airport surcharge applies because this trip terminates at Blk 420 Woodlands St 41 and does not ORIGINATE at Changi or Seletar. POL-RD-09 therefore contributes nothing to the rider's remedy, there is no phantom or unmatched line for POL-RD-09(4) to refund, and no billing-integrity referral arises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02830", "EV-TRIP-02830"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is unimpaired on the policy test as well as the schema test: 181 fixes at a 10 s sampling interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps and a maximum inter-fix gap of 0.0 s, so none of POL-RD-07's limbs (a) to (c) fires. The excess is therefore a measured fact and not an estimate, no impairment discount applies, and the POL-RD-10(3) escalation route is closed on this record: the case is decidable at the measured 6.25 km excess.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02830"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own account of an expressway jam cannot be run on this record and discharges nothing. The only traffic advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-02830-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - no advisory covers the Blk 640 Jurong West St 61 corridor in this window - so POL-RD-03's requirement of an advisory naming a road or segment the optimal route traverses, carrying a validity window overlapping the trace time and matched by a route that leaves and rejoins the optimal corridor, has no record to test against; and under POL-RD-08 an assertion that cites no traffic_advisory ID carries no weight. POL-RD-13(1) fixes the consequence: because the driver names no advisory evidence ID, the absent advisory is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a missing artifact within POL-RD-10(5), so the case resolves as money on the measured excess rather than being held for a reviewer.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02830-01", "EV-GPS-02830"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 6.8,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the charge for trip TRP-02830 is partly refunded. Distance. The GPS trace EV-GPS-02830 measures 22.95 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against a booked optimal route of 16.7 km on the trip record EV-TRIP-02830. The excess is 6.25 km, or 37.4%, and both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (over 0.8 km and over 20% of optimal), so a route deviation is established on the trace figure, which POL-RD-01 makes governing over the rounded 22.9 km convenience copy. Neither materiality test is met (6.25 km is below 8.0 km; 37.4% is below 50%), so this is not a MATERIAL deviation, the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not engaged, and no POL-RD-06(b) uplift or POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises. For completeness, the two counters POL-RD-06 names show no pattern in any event (deviation_flags_90d of 1 against completed_trips_90d of 395, a rate of 0.0025), and the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used. The trace is unimpaired on the policy test as well as the schema test: 181 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum inter-fix gap of 0.0 s, so none of POL-RD-07(a) to (c) fires and the POL-RD-10(3) escalation route is closed. Refund. The fare breakdown EV-FARE-02830 shows a METERED fare, so POL-RD-02 applies. charged_total is 30.18. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 16.7 + 0.28 x 22.5) x the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, plus the 0.80 platform fee, with no ERP, tolls, fixed surcharge, waiting-time fee or promo discount = 23.425. Refund = 30.18 - 23.425 = 6.755, rounded UP to a payable SGD 6.80. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and 22.4% of charged_total, far below the 90% share that would convert the outcome to a full refund, so the result is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 6.80 against the 8.50 claimed. Pass-through lines. POL-RD-09 adds and subtracts nothing: erp_lines total 0.00 with no off-optimal-route gantry charged, no tolls, no waiting-time fee, and no airport surcharge because this trip ends at Blk 420 Woodlands St 41 and does not originate at an airport. There is no phantom or unmatched charge line, so no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral arises. The driver's traffic explanation. The driver's account of a jam on the expressway is discarded. The bundle holds no traffic advisory for this trip: EV-ADVIS-02830-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT (no advisory covers the Blk 640 Jurong West St 61 corridor in this window). Under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08 the assertion cannot be tested, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the excuse carries no weight. Because the driver names no advisory evidence ID, POL-RD-13(1) keeps POL-RD-10(5) from firing: this is a gap in the bundle, not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so the case is decided on the measured excess and money moves rather than being held. Other routes out. POL-RD-04 gives the driver nothing: the chat log EV-CHAT-02830 is empty (0 messages, both timestamps null), so there is no rider instruction, waypoint or requested road, and POL-RD-14 has nothing to operate on. POL-RD-05 gives no re-quote: pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so the booked 16.7 km optimal governs. POL-RD-12 does not apply: vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, and solo_optimal_distance_km is null. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires and no referral is produced by any clause. The ruling rests on artifacts all at weight 1.0, so confidence is 0.95. The monetary effect of SGD 6.80 is at or below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so this provisional ruling is executed automatically. This ruling was made without human review; either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "No POL-RD-10 trigger fires and this case should be ruled, not escalated. The trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07; the timestamps run forward and no two admitted artifacts disagree - pickup 17:08:27 on the trace against 17:08:27 on the trip_record, ended 17:38:27 against charged 17:38:52; the refund of 6.755 is far below both the SGD 150.00 ceiling and charged_total; every charge line has a counterpart in the trip_record; and the driver's traffic excuse is a failed assertion rather than contradictory evidence of comparable strength, per POL-RD-13(1).",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02830-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

